==Location and Uses==
==={{OoA|-}}===
Diamonds are rhomboidal [[Block]]s that appear throughout [[Labrynna]] and its [[Dungeon]]s. When hit with the [[Switch Hook]] or [[Long Hook]], they will switch places with [[Link]]. They are often used as elements of [[Switching Puzzle]]s, sometimes to impress [[Switch]]es into the floor.

==={{BotW|-}}===
Diamonds are rare [[Material]]s in {{BotW}}. Because of their rarity, Diamonds have long been sold for a high price in [[Hyrule]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> [[Ramella]], the [[Gerudo]] in [[Goron City]], may offer to buy Diamonds from Link at a 10% increase of the regular sale price, trading a bulk of 10 Diamonds for 5,500 [[Rupee]]s instead of the regular total of 5,000.<ref>{{Cite|By the way, do you happen to have {{Color BotW|Red|10 diamonds}}? You'll get 5,000 rupees if you sell them at a store... or you can trade them to me for {{Color BotW|Red|5,500 rupees}}.|Ramella|BotW}}</ref> Diamonds can be used as an ingredient for [[White Dye]] at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]]. If [[Link]] uses Diamonds while [[Cooking]], the resulting meal will be [[Rock-Hard Food]].

Link can obtain Diamonds by breaking [[Ore Deposit]]s and [[Rare Ore Deposit]]s. They also have a chance to drop after slaying [[Stone Talus (Rare)|Stone Taluses (Rare)]], [[Frost Talus]]es, [[Igneo Talus]]es, or Silver and Golden [[Enemy|Enemies]]. [[Kairo]], the traveling [[Goron]] [[Merchant]], will sell Diamonds during unusual weather.<ref>{{Cite|This weather has me in a rare mood to sell rare ore. How about a {{Color BotW|Red|diamond}}? You interested in rare items?|Kairo|BotW}}</ref> The only other place that sells Diamonds is [[Ore and More]] in [[Tarrey Town]].

Diamonds can be found inside [[Treasure Chest]]s in the following [[Ancient Shrine]]s:
* [[Bareeda Naag Shrine]]
* [[Gee Ha'rah Shrine]]
* [[Kaam Ya'tak Shrine]]
* [[Kah Mael Shrine]]
* [[Keeha Yoog Shrine]]
* [[Maka Rah Shrine]]
* [[Misae Suma Shrine]]
* [[Mozo Shenno Shrine]]

Diamonds may spawn when the following [[amiibo]] are scanned used the [[Amiibo (Ability)|amiibo]] [[Rune]]:
* {{SSB|-}} series [[Ganondorf]]
* {{SSB|-}} series [[Princess Zelda|Zelda]]
* {{TLoZ|-}} series [[Zelda]]
* {{BotW|-}} series [[Princess Zelda|Zelda]]
* {{BotW|-}} series [[Mipha]]
* {{BotW|-}} series [[Revali]]
* {{BotW|-}} series [[Daruk]]
* {{BotW|-}} series [[Urbosa]]

Several [[Side Quest]]s offer Diamonds as a reward.{{Note|If Link has a maximum of 999 Diamonds in his [[Inventory]] and is offered one as a reward, the gifter will hold onto it until he has made room.<ref>{{Cite|Or...I'd like to, but you currently don't have room for {{Color BotW|Red|two more}} {{Color BotW|Blue|diamonds}}.|Ledo|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Well... I'd like to, anyway, but you don't currently have room for {{Color BotW|Red|one more}} {{Color BotW|Blue|diamond}}.|Ledo|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Well, I want to give them to you, but it looks like you haven't got room for {{Color BotW|Red|three}} {{Color BotW|Blue|diamonds}}.|Hudson|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|I would like to reward you, but it seems you already have quite a collection of {{Color BotW|Blue|diamonds}}. Since you cannot carry any more, I suggest you somehow rid yourself of one and come back.|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Hmm? You are overflowing with diamonds! I was gonna give you some diamonds for solving my riddles, but... Z z z z z...|Walton|BotW}}</ref>}} Link can obtain a Diamond from [[Pirou]] by trading him 55 [[Rushroom]]s during the "[[Rushroom Rush!]]" Side Quest.<ref>{{Cite|I'll give a {{Color BotW|Red|diamond}} for {{Color BotW|Blue|55 rushrooms}}. That's worth the effort, right?|Pirou|BotW}}</ref> [[Ledo]] will reward Link with two Diamonds for bringing him the 10 [[Luminous Stone]]s needed to repair [[Zora's Domain]] during "[[Luminous Stone Gathering]]".<ref>{{Cite|Oh, that's right... I must reward you!|Ledo|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|And what's more, I'll give you {{Color BotW|Red|one}} extra as a bonus!|Ledo|BotW}}</ref> Afterwards, Ledo will continue to trade Link one Diamond in exchange for 10 Luminous Stones.<ref>{{Cite|If you ever find yourself in possession of {{Color BotW|Red|10}} {{Color BotW|Blue|luminous stones}} in the future, I hope you will bring them to me. But if that happens, know that I'll only be able to give you {{Color BotW|Red|one}} {{Color BotW|Blue|diamond}} for them. I would be honored if you would accept it when the time comes!|Ledo|BotW}}</ref> Three Diamonds are also received from [[Hudson]] as a reward for completing "[[From the Ground Up]]",<ref>{{Cite|And now {{Color BotW|Blue|Tarrey Town}} looks like a real town at long last. This was all possible because of you. I can't thank you enough for all the hard work you did. All right. This is for you.|Hudson|BotW}}</ref> which were found while clearing the land for Tarrey Town.<ref>{{Cite|These were found inside the boulders we smashed when we were clearing land. Rhondson and I have no use for them. You can take them.|Hudson|BotW}}</ref> [[Jiahto]] will pay Link one Diamond in return for helping to archive the [[Zora]] legends upon the [[Stone Monument]]s scattered around the [[Lanayru Great Spring]] as part of the "[[Zora Stone Monuments]]" Side Quest.<ref>{{Cite|Hmm... The history, culture, folkore, and various heroic acts of the proud Zora people... It's all here! Eureka! Thanks to you, I've compiled the precious information from those stone monuments! Link, thank you for taking on such an arduous task! Please, allow me to reward you!|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref> A Diamond is the reward for completing the "[[Riddles of Hyrule]]" Side Quest, tasked by [[Walton]] in the [[Korok Forest]].<ref>{{Cite|I knew you could do it, Mr. Hero! Here is your reward!|Walton|BotW}}</ref> Finally, a Diamond is the final reward in the series of requests that [[Nebb]] has for Link in [[Hateno Village]] as part of "[[The Weapon Connoisseur]]" Side Quest,<ref>{{Cite|Thanks! Here's a token of my thanks!|Nebb|BotW}}</ref> which was entrusted to him by his grandfather.<ref>{{Cite|That was from my grandpa. He always said, "Give it to the one who can show you the real deal." So don't worry about it! Thanks for showing me so many things! I'm sure my grandpa is super happy...wherever he is! Bye!|Nebb|BotW}}</ref>

Diamonds are required for [[Isha]] to craft [[Diamond Circlet]]s at [[Starlight Memories]] in [[Gerudo Town]]. Diamonds are also necessary to repair the [[Weapon]]s used by the late [[Champions]], these being Mipha's [[Lightscale Trident]],<ref>{{Cite|In that case, I will need a {{Color BotW|Blue|Zora Spear}}, {{Color BotW|Red|one}} {{Color BotW|Blue|diamond}}, and {{Color BotW|Red|five pieces}} of {{Color BotW|Blue|flint}}.|Dento|BotW}}</ref> Revali's [[Great Eagle Bow]],<ref>{{Cite|If you want me to make another one, I will need a {{Color BotW|Blue|swallow bow}}, a {{Color BotW|Blue|diamond}}, and {{Color BotW|Red|five}} bundles of {{Color BotW|Blue|wood}}.|Harth|BotW}}</ref> Daruk's [[Boulder Breaker]],<ref>{{Cite|If ya want a new one, I'm gonna need a {{Color BotW|Blue|cobble crusher}}, {{Color BotW|Red|five pieces}} of {{Color BotW|Blue|flint}}, and a {{Color BotW|Blue|diamond}}.|Rohan|BotW}}</ref> and Urbosa's [[Scimitar of the Seven]] and [[Daybreaker]].<ref>{{Cite|The {{Color BotW|Red|Scimitar of the Seven}}, huh? To make it, I'll need {{Color BotW|Blue|one diamond}}, {{Color BotW|Blue|five}} pieces of {{Color BotW|Blue|flint}}, and a {{Color BotW|Blue|Gerudo scimitar}}.|Buliara|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|The {{Color BotW|Red|Daybreaker}}, huh? To make it, I'll need {{Color BotW|Blue|one diamond}}, {{Color BotW|Blue|five}} pieces of {{Color BotW|Blue|flint}}, and a {{Color BotW|Blue|Gerudo shield}}.|Buliara|BotW}}</ref> These can be repaired by [[Dento]], [[Harth]], [[Rohan]], and [[Buliara]], respectively.

Diamonds are required to upgrade the [[Diamond Circlet]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|BotW|Diamond}}

==={{TotK|-}}===
Diamonds are sharp [[Material]]s in {{TotK}}. They can be [[Fuse]]d onto [[Weapon]]s or [[Arrow]]s to increase their damage by 25.

Diamonds are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|TotK|Diamond}}

==Other Appearances==
==={{ZA|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
[[File:ZA Diamond Sprite.png|left]]
The Diamond is obtained by giving the [[Coal]] to the Blacksmith in [[Great Wimbich]]. Receiving the Diamond automatically rewards Zelda with 999 Rupees. It is kept in the inventory afterwards, but has no other use.
{{Noncanon|End}}

==={{CoH|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
{{Stub|CoH}}
Diamonds are a currency similar to Rupees. They can be used to purchase various Items in shops in the Hyrule. Unlike Rupees, Diamonds will not be lost if the characters get a game over.<ref>{{Cite|Unlike rupees and keys, {{Color CoH|Yellow|diamonds}} won't be lost when you get a game over.|Trill (Cadence of Hyrule)|CoH}}</ref> Diamonds can be obtained by defeating all enemies on a screen,<ref>{{Cite|Diamonds will drop only once the {{Color CoH|Blue|last enemy}} on a screen is defeated.|Trill (Cadence of Hyrule)|CoH}}</ref> or finding them in dungeons or chests.
{{Noncanon|End}}

==={{AoC|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
In {{AoC|-}} hold a close resemblance to the ones in {{BotW|-}}. They can be bought at the store in the [[Gerudo Desert]], or be found in gray [[Treasure Chest]]s in main quests. They can be sold to most [[Merchant]]s for 500 [[Rupee]]s, but [[Dayfah]] will buy them for 1,250 Rupees.
{{Noncanon|End}}

